('Rest Is Not Laziness',
 'stress',
 'In the midst of stress and anxiety, it''s easy to feel guilty for slowing down. Yet, Scripture reminds us that rest is a gift from God—not a sign of weakness or laziness. Jesus Himself invited us to come away and find rest for our souls (Matthew 11:28). Embracing rest allows our minds and bodies to reset so we can face challenges with renewed strength and peace.',
 'Today, set aside at least 20 minutes to intentionally rest—whether through prayer, quiet reflection, or simply pausing from your tasks. Treat this time as sacred, not optional.',
 'How might allowing yourself regular rest change the way you handle stress and anxiety in your life?',
 'In a world that often equates busyness with worth, it can be difficult to accept rest as essential rather than indulgent. Yet God modeled rest from the very beginning, instituting the Sabbath as a holy pause (Genesis 2:2-3). Jesus echoed this rhythm, inviting us to come to Him for rest when overwhelmed (Matthew 11:28-30). When anxiety floods our mind, rest is not a luxury but a necessity—an act of trust that God holds our burdens. It is during these moments of stillness that we allow God''s peace to flood in, calming our...''s gentle reassurance. This rest equips us to face life''s storms with clarity and resilience, reminding...''s love. Today, consider how inviting rest into your routine might transform your response to stress and anxiety, grounding you more deeply in God''s sustaining grace.',
 ARRAY['rest', 'sabbath', 'burnout', 'anxiety'],
 'published',
 CURRENT_DATE + INTERVAL '7 days',
 false,
 8),

('The Weight of Tomorrow',
