 'It''s easy to feel overwhelmed by the...''s grace sufficient for now. Trusting Him with the weight of tomorrow lightens our load today.',
 'Today, practice anchoring yourself in the present by taking three mindful breaths whenever you notice anxiety creeping in about the future. Remind yourself gently, ''I will trust God with tomorrow, and I can face today with His strength.''',
 'What is one worry about the future that I can surrender to God right now, trusting Him to carry it for me?',
 'Anxiety about the future can feel like carrying a heavy backpack filled with unknown fears and what-ifs. Yet, Jesus offers an invitation to lay down that burden by living fully in the present. Matthew 6:34 counsels us, (Matthew 6:34) This doesn''t mean ignoring planning or responsibility but...''s weight to God, we create space to receive His grace for today. It''s a daily discipline of trust—reminding ourselves that God''s faithfulness is not limited and that...''s needs with courage and calm. By focusing on what we can do and leaving the outcomes to God, we find freedom and hope that sustains us through uncertainty.',
