('When the Body Keeps Score',
 'stress',
 'Stress and anxiety often manifest not just in our minds but deeply within our bodies. When we ignore the subtle signals—tight shoulders, shallow breath, racing heart—we miss an important language God uses to tell us to slow down and seek rest. Scripture reminds us to cast all our anxieties on Him because He cares for us (1 Peter 5:7). By tuning into our physical state, we can better recognize when to pause and invite God''s peace.',
 'Today, take five minutes to check in with your body. Notice any areas of tension or discomfort without judgment. Breathe deeply and pray, asking God to help you release anxiety and restore calm. Consider journaling what your body reveals to you as a form of spiritual awareness.',
 'How does your body communicate stress to you, and how might listening to it open a deeper path to God''s peace?',
 'Our bodies often carry the hidden burdens of stress and anxiety, long before our minds fully grasp what we''re experiencing. Neuroscientist Bessel van der Kolk...''s design of body, mind, and spirit. The Apostle Paul encourages us not to be anxious but to present our requests to God with thanksgiving (Philippians 4:6-7), promising peace that surpasses understanding to guard our hearts and minds. Practically, this means learning to recognize bodily cues as God''s gentle signals urging us toward rest...''s comfort to move through us, helping us break the cycle of stress. Today, let your body be a gateway to deeper faith, acknowledging that caring for it is also an act of worship and trust in God''s sustaining grace.',
 ARRAY['physical stress', 'body awareness', 'anxiety', 'faith and healing'],
 'published',
