('Perfectionism Is a Prison',
 'stress',
 'Perfectionism can trap us in a cycle of stress and anxiety, convincing us that nothing we do is ever enough. Yet Scripture reminds us that God''s grace is sufficient, and His power is made perfect in our weakness (2 Corinthians 12:9). Instead of striving for flawless control, we can rest in the truth that we are already loved and accepted just as we are. Letting go of perfectionism opens the door to peace and freedom.',
 'Today, try to identify one area where you tend to demand perfection from yourself. Give yourself permission to do just enough or to make a small mistake without judgment. Remind yourself of God''s grace by reading 2 Corinthians 12:9 aloud and reflecting on what it means for your daily pressures.',
 'Where in your life are you holding yourself to impossible standards, and how might God''s grace invite you to let go?',
 'Perfectionism often masquerades as discipline or high standards, but it can quickly become a prison that breeds stress and anxiety. When we define our worth by flawless performance, we set ourselves up for constant disappointment and exhaustion. The Bible offers a tender but powerful reminder: God''s grace is enough. In 2 Corinthians 12:9, Paul shares that Christ''s power is made perfect in weakness, which means our imperfections don''t disqualify us—they actually create space for God''s strength to shine through. Embracing grace means accepting that we don''t have to earn God''s love by being perfect, and neither...''s freedom and love. What would it look like to trust that you are enough, just as you are?',
 ARRAY['perfectionism', 'grace', 'enough', 'stress'],
 'published',
 CURRENT_DATE + INTERVAL '10 days',
 false,
