('The Gift of Limits',
 'stress',
 'In our fast-paced world, stress and anxiety often stem from trying to do too much and saying yes when we need to say no. God teaches us the beauty of boundaries—limits that protect our well-being and enable us to serve from a place of strength. Embracing these limits is not a failure but a gift that invites peace into our lives.',
 'Today, identify one area where you feel overwhelmed and practice saying ''no'' or setting a clear boundary. Notice how this small act of self-care helps reduce your stress and restores your focus.',
 'Where in your life might God be inviting you to embrace limits and say no for your own peace and health?',
 'Stress and anxiety can feel like persistent shadows, following us through every task and interaction. Yet, Scripture gently reminds us of the importance of boundaries and rest, highlighting God''s design for our lives. In Psalm...''s strength into our weakness. This act of self-care is not selfish; it''s an essential part of how we live out our faith authentically. Today, reflect on the areas where you may be overextending yourself and trust that embracing these limits is a way of honoring God with your life and health.',
 ARRAY['boundaries', 'saying no', 'self-care', 'stress'],
 'published',
