 'The illusion of busyness is a common trap in today''s culture, especially when stress and anxiety...''Be still, and know that I am God.'' This stillness is not inactivity but a spiritual posture—pausing to recognize God''s presence and sovereignty amid life''s chaos. When we allow ourselves to step back from the constant rush, we create space to hear God''s voice, receive His peace, and remember...''t mean neglecting responsibilities but intentionally balancing action with rest, trusting that God is at work even when we are still. Today''s challenge is to break free from...''s invitation to rest, renewing our strength and calming our anxious hearts.',
