('Carrying Others'' Burdens',
 'stress',
 'It''s natural to want to help those weighed down by stress and anxiety, but continually carrying others'' burdens can wear us thin. Galatians 6:2 encourages us to ''bear one another''s burdens,'' yet it''s also important to recognize our limits and set healthy boundaries. Compassion doesn''t mean sacrificing our own well-being; it means loving others in sustainable ways. Today, embrace empathy with wisdom, allowing God to refresh your heart as you support those around you.',
 'Take a moment today to assess how much emotional energy you''re investing in others'' struggles. If it feels overwhelming, gently communicate your limits and ask for God''s strength to maintain healthy boundaries while still offering care.',
 'In what areas might I be overextending myself emotionally, and how can I invite God to help me balance compassion with self-care?',
 'Caring deeply for others is a beautiful reflection of Christ''s love, yet it can lead to empathy fatigue when we don''t protect our own hearts. Galatians 6:2 calls us to ''bear one another''s burdens,'' but it doesn''t mean bearing them alone or beyond...''s essential to establish boundaries that keep us grounded in God''s peace. Compassion paired with wisdom allows...''s grace is sufficient for you—lean on Him to carry the weight alongside you. By protecting your well-being, you create a sustainable way to reflect Christ''s love that honors both yourself and others.',
