 'Where in my life am I holding myself to impossible standards, and how might I invite God''s grace into that struggle?',
 'Stress and anxiety often stem from our relentless desire to appear in control and meet every expectation flawlessly. This pursuit can lead to a heavy burden of shame when we fall short. However, the Bible offers a profound counterpoint: our weaknesses are not reasons for despair but opportunities for God''s strength to shine through. In 2 Corinthians 12:9, Paul shares that God''s grace is sufficient and His power...''t a sign of failure but a doorway to deeper authenticity and peace. When we stop hiding behind masks of perfection, we create space to experience God''s unconditional love and healing. Today, let''s remember that courage isn''t the absence of anxiety but the...''s enduring grace.',
