('The Spiral of What-If',
 'stress',
 'When stress and anxiety take hold, our minds often spiral into a web of ''what-if'' scenarios, imagining worst-case outcomes that may never come to pass. This pattern, known as catastrophizing, feeds our fears and clouds our peace. Yet, Scripture reminds us in Philippians 4:6-7 to present our anxieties to God through prayer, trusting His peace to guard our hearts. Choosing to pause and redirect our thoughts can break the cycle of rumination and invite calm into our day.',
 'Today, when you catch yourself drifting into ''what-if''thinking, gently stop and write down your...''s Word or a positive affirmation grounded in faith. This practice helps train your mind to focus on God''s promises rather than imagined troubles.',
 'What ''what-if'' thoughts have taken over your mind recently, and how might inviting God into those worries change your perspective?',
 'The spiral of ''what-if''thinking is a common trap that fuels...''t dependent on circumstances but on trusting God''s sovereignty and goodness. Breaking free from...''s presence is a refuge in the storm of anxious thoughts, inviting you to rest in Him rather than in fear. Today, lean into His promises and let His peace quiet the spiral.',
 ARRAY['catastrophizing', 'rumination', 'thought patterns', 'stress and anxiety'],
 'published',
