('When Everything Feels Heavy',
 'stress',
 'Life can sometimes feel unbearably heavy, with stress and anxiety pressing down on our hearts. In those moments, it''s important to remember that we are never truly alone—God invites us to cast our burdens on Him, as He cares deeply for us (1 Peter 5:7). Though the weight may not immediately lift, hope can anchor our souls and remind us that relief and peace are possible.',
 'Today, take five minutes to pause and breathe deeply. As you do, quietly invite God into your worries, naming one specific concern and asking Him to carry it with you. Write it down and then physically set the paper aside as a symbolic act of surrender.',
 'What is one worry or burden you can give over to God today, trusting He cares for you deeply?',
 'When stress and anxiety overwhelm us, it''s easy to feel isolated, as if...''t a simplistic promise that problems vanish instantly but a powerful reminder that we don''t have to carry our burdens alone. God''s care provides a firm foundation amid life''s storms. Practically, this means creating space...''s presence sustains and strengthens us. Today, leaning into this hope can transform how we face stress—moving from isolation to connection, from overwhelm to surrender. Remember, healing often begins with the small, intentional act of handing over one worry at a time, trusting God''s unfailing love.',
 ARRAY['overwhelm', 'anxiety', 'hope', 'depression'],
 'published',
