('The Practice of Gratitude',
 'stress',
 'When anxiety feels overwhelming, turning our focus toward gratitude can shift our perspective profoundly. Scripture reminds us in 1 Thessalonians 5:18 to give thanks in all circumstances, not just the easy ones. This practice doesn''t erase stress but invites joy and peace to coexist with our struggles. Gratitude helps us see God''s presence even in the chaos.',
 'Today, write down three specific things you are grateful for, especially amidst current challenges. Reflect on how these blessings impact your life and invite a moment of quiet thanksgiving.',
 'What is one small blessing you might have overlooked today that could bring you peace if you acknowledged it?',
 'Stress and anxiety often cloud our vision, making it hard to see beyond immediate worries. Yet, cultivating gratitude can be a powerful spiritual practice that recalibrates our hearts and minds. In Philippians 4:6-7, Paul encourages us to present our requests to God with thanksgiving, promising a peace that surpasses understanding. This peace doesn''t mean problems disappear but transforms how we face them. Gratitude shifts our focus from what''s lacking to what''s present — from fear to faith. It opens our eyes to God''s daily mercies and strengthens our resilience....''s sustaining love.',
 ARRAY['gratitude', 'perspective', 'joy', 'faith'],
 'published',
