 'Today, take a moment to write down one plan that isn''t going as expected. Offer it up to God in prayer, asking Him to guide your steps and help you embrace flexibility rather than frustration.',
 'How might surrendering control over your plans open you to new possibilities God wants to show you?',
 'When our plans fall apart, it often triggers a cascade of anxiety and disappointment. We invest so much effort in mapping out the future, only to be blindsided by unexpected changes. Yet, the Bible offers profound comfort in these times. Proverbs 3:5-6 calls us to trust in the Lord wholeheartedly and not depend solely on our own insight. This trust does not imply passivity but invites active surrender — a courageous choice to release control and accept God''s greater wisdom. By embracing flexibility, we make space for God to work in ways we hadn''t imagined. It''s a process that can be deeply...''s way of redirecting us toward a better path. Today''s challenge is to lean into that uncertainty with faith rather than fear.',
