('Wisdom vs. Knowledge',
 'decisions',
 'When faced with difficult decisions, it''s easy to rely solely on what...''s will and understanding the heart behind the facts. Proverbs 3:5-6 reminds us to trust in the Lord with all our heart, not leaning on our own understanding. True wisdom invites us to pause, pray, and seek God''s guidance, especially when choices feel overwhelming.',
 'Today, when you encounter a challenging decision, take a moment to pause and pray for God''s wisdom before acting. Write down what you know, then ask God to help you see beyond the facts and understand His path for you.',
 'In what areas of your life are you leaning too heavily on knowledge alone, and how might inviting God''s wisdom change your perspective?',
 'Difficult decisions often tempt us to depend on knowledge—what we can see, know, and analyze. However, wisdom, as Scripture teaches, is a deeper, God-given insight that aligns our choices with His purpose and timing. Proverbs 2:6 says, ''For the Lord gives wisdom; from his mouth come knowledge and understanding.''This highlights that knowledge without divine wisdom...''s plan amid uncertainty. In practice, this means seeking God through prayer, listening to His voice in Scripture, and being open to the guidance of the Holy Spirit. Wisdom also involves patience, as God''s timing often differs from ours. By prioritizing wisdom over mere knowledge, we gain clarity and peace that surpasses human understanding, enabling us to navigate hard choices with confidence and faith.',
 ARRAY['wisdom', 'discernment', 'understanding', 'faith'],
 'published',
