 false,
 14),

('Seeking Counsel Wisely',
 'decisions',
 'When faced with difficult decisions, it''s easy to feel overwhelmed and isolated. Yet, Proverbs reminds us, ''Without counsel plans fail, but with many advisers they succeed''(Proverbs 15:22). Seeking wisdom from trusted mentors...''s guidance. Remember, wise counsel is not just advice but a reflection of God''s love working through others.',
 'Today, identify one trustworthy person—whether a mentor, friend, or spiritual leader—and share your current challenge with them. Invite their insight and listen prayerfully to their perspective, discerning what aligns with God''s truth.',
 'Who in your life reflects God''s wisdom and love well enough that you feel safe seeking their counsel during tough decisions?',
 'Difficult decisions often feel like crossroads where every option carries uncertainty and risk. In these moments, seeking counsel wisely becomes vital. The Bible encourages us to gather many advisers, not because human wisdom is perfect, but because God often speaks through the community He places around us. It''s important to approach counsel with discernment—choosing...''s grace through others. Besides gaining practical advice, this communal process can reveal God''s heart and guidance we might have...''s voice amid many opinions and trust that He is present in the journey, shaping your decisions for your good and His glory.',
