('The Courage to Change Course',
 'decisions',
 'Making difficult decisions often requires the bravery to acknowledge when a path isn''t leading us where we hoped. Like...''s guidance even when it means admitting mistakes. Growth comes not from stubbornness but from the humility to change course. Remember, God''s grace meets us in those moments of uncertainty.',
 'Today, take time to reflect on a decision you''ve been hesitant to revisit. Pray for courage and clarity, then write down one small step you can take to pivot or adjust your direction if needed.',
 'What is one area in your life where you need the courage to admit a mistake and change course?',
 'Difficult decisions often test our faith more than we realize. It''s tempting to cling to what feels familiar, even when it''s clear the road ahead isn''t right. The story of Moses reminds...''t a sign of failure but a step toward deeper wisdom and alignment with God''s purpose. In Proverbs 3:5-6, we are...''s natural to feel fear or doubt, but God''s grace empowers us to take steps forward with confidence. Today''s challenge is to embrace humility and lean into His guidance, knowing that changing course can lead to unexpected blessings and spiritual growth.',
