 'How can I better consider the needs and feelings of others when making difficult choices?',
 'Difficult decisions that affect others carry a heavy weight because they require more than just personal preference; they demand empathy, responsibility, and a heart tuned to God''s wisdom. Scripture encourages us to lean...''s natural to feel the burden of responsibility, but God doesn''t call us to navigate these moments alone. When we invite Him into our decision-making process, He can grant insight beyond our limited view. Today, as you face decisions that affect others, try to listen deeply—to God and to the people involved—and act with love and humility. This approach not only honors those impacted but also reflects the heart of Christ, who always considers others first.',
