('Deciding to Forgive',
 'decisions',
 'Choosing to forgive is one of the hardest decisions we face, especially when hurt runs deep. Yet, Jesus reminds us in Matthew 6:14 that forgiveness is essential not just for others, but for our own freedom. Holding onto pain can weigh us down, but releasing it through forgiveness opens the door to healing and peace. It''s a courageous step toward restoring your heart.',
 'Today, identify one person or situation you''ve been holding onto resentment toward. Write...''s just a small start. Pray for strength to take that first step toward release.',
 'What is one hurt you''ve been unwilling to forgive, and how might letting go change your heart and your life?',
 'Forgiveness is often misunderstood as excusing wrongdoing or forgetting the pain caused. In reality, it''s a deliberate decision to release the...''s not always instantaneous or easy; forgiveness can be a process requiring prayer, reflection, and sometimes professional support. But every small step toward forgiveness is a step toward healing. By deciding to forgive, you open yourself to God''s peace that surpasses understanding and invite restoration both inwardly and in your relationships. Today, let that decision be a courageous act of faith, trusting God to guide your heart toward wholeness.',
