('When to Wait and When to Act',
 'decisions',
 'Life often places us at crossroads where the choice between waiting and acting feels overwhelming. Scripture reminds us in Ecclesiastes 3:1 that there is a season for every purpose under heaven—a time to be still and a time to move forward. Trusting God''s timing requires patience, but faith also...''s guidance.',
 'Today, take a quiet moment to ask God for clarity on a decision you''re facing. Write down what you feel prompted to do—whether it''s to wait, pray more, seek counsel, or take a concrete step forward. Commit to trusting God''s timing rather than rushing or delaying unnecessarily.',
 'How can I better recognize God''s timing in my decisions and distinguish between fear-driven delays and faithful waiting?',
 'When confronted with difficult decisions, it''s natural to wrestle between the urge...''s plan. Ecclesiastes 3:1 teaches us there is an appointed time for every activity under heaven, encouraging us to seek God''s timing rather than our own. Waiting...''s ahead. Yet, faith also calls for decisive action when God opens the door. The challenge lies in discerning the difference—between procrastination driven by fear and faithful patience surrendered to God''s will. This discernment grows through prayer,...''s prompting, we find peace in both waiting and acting. Today''s journey is about embracing that tension, knowing that God''s timing is perfect even when ours is not.',
