('The Myth of the Perfect Decision',
 'decisions',
 'When faced with difficult decisions, it''s easy to fall into the trap of seeking the perfect choice, as if there''s one flawless path. Yet, Scripture reminds us that God''s grace covers our imperfections and that...''good enough'' can lead to meaningful progress. Trusting God''s guidance allows us to move forward, even when certainty is elusive.',
