 'What is one decision you''ve been holding onto because you want it to be perfect, and how might embracing ''good enough'' free you to move forward?',
 'In our journey of faith, we often wrestle with the pressure to make the perfect decision, believing that one wrong step could derail our lives. This mindset mirrors the perfectionism that can trap us in fear and indecision. Yet, the Bible offers a different perspective. Proverbs 3:5-6 encourages us to trust in the Lord with all our heart and lean not on our own understanding, promising that He will direct our paths. This means that while we seek wisdom and discernment, God''s grace fills in the gaps when our choices fall short of perfection. Decisions don''t have to be flawless to be...''good enough''allows us to act in faith rather...''s faithfulness in guiding us through every twist and turn.',
