('Deciding What to Let Go',
 'decisions',
 'Life often calls us to make hard choices about what to keep and what to release. Like decluttering a crowded room, deciding what to let go can create space for God to move more freely in our hearts. Scripture reminds us in Philippians 3:13 to forget what lies behind and strain forward to what lies ahead. Trusting God with our priorities helps us focus on what truly matters.',
 'Today, identify one thing—be it an activity, a worry, or a possession—that is weighing you down or distracting you from your purpose, and take a concrete step to let it go, whether by donating, delegating, or simply deciding not to engage with it.',
 'What is one thing in my life I''ve been holding onto out of fear or comfort that God might be asking me to release?',
 'Making difficult decisions about what to let go is a deeply spiritual practice as much as a practical one. Jesus calls us to take up our cross and follow Him, which often means surrendering the familiar and uncomfortable attachments that hold us back. Decluttering our lives isn''t just about physical possessions, but also...''s challenge is to courageously evaluate what no longer serves your journey and entrust it to God’s care, trusting that He will guide you to what truly enriches your life and faith.',
