('When Others Disagree',
 'decisions',
 'Making difficult decisions often means facing disagreement from those we care about. It''s natural to want everyone to agree, but following God''s guidance sometimes requires us to stand firm in our convictions, even when it''s uncomfortable. Jesus Himself faced opposition when He chose to follow His Father''s will. Remember, peace comes not from pleasing everyone, but from aligning with God''s truth.',
