 'In what areas of your life are you tempted to prioritize people''s approval over God''s direction, and how can you begin to shift that balance?',
 'Difficult decisions become even more challenging when they create tension with those around us. It''s painful when loved ones disagree or...''t a sign of failure; they can be a sign that we are stepping out in faith. Jesus Himself faced rejection when He chose to fulfill God''s plan, showing us that conviction sometimes requires standing alone. People-pleasing might seem easier, but it often leads us away from the peace God intends. Instead, we are called to seek His wisdom above all, trusting that He will guide us and use even opposition for our growth. Embracing this truth can bring peace amid conflict, reminding us that true approval comes from God, not man.',
