('Trusting God with the Outcome',
 'decisions',
 'Making difficult decisions often leaves us feeling vulnerable and uncertain. It''s natural to want to control every...''s peace and guidance through the unknown. Even when the path is unclear, faith invites us to lean into God''s sovereignty rather than our own understanding.',
 'Today, take a moment to write down one decision that feels heavy or uncertain. Pray over it, asking God for wisdom and peace, then consciously surrender the outcome to Him by saying, ''Lord, I trust You with this.'' Let go of the need to control and notice how this act of surrender affects your heart throughout the day.',
 'What is one area in your life where you struggle to trust God with the outcome, and what might it look like to surrender that fully to Him?',
 'Difficult decisions are some of the most challenging moments in our lives. They often come with pressure, fear, and the temptation to control every detail ourselves. Yet the Bible invites us into a different posture—one of surrender and trust. Proverbs 3:5-6 encourages us to (Proverbs 3:5-6) Trusting God with the outcome doesn''t mean passivity; it means actively seeking...''s about choosing faith over fear, remembering that God''s plans for us are good, even...''s faithful presence.',
 ARRAY['surrender', 'faith', 'control', 'trust'],
 'published',
